  "_ai_update_prompt": "You are updating THE JERSEY GAME dataset.\n\nThis JSON file is the source of truth for jersey puzzle records used by minigames/jersey/index.html. Team identity, display market, sport, palette, mascot, fanbase, and TGBID metadata come from db/teams.json at runtime. Return ONLY the complete valid JSON object with this same structure. Do not return SQL, Markdown, commentary, or a partial patch.\n\nJSON structure:\n- _ai_update_prompt: these durable update instructions.\n- generatedAt: timestamp for the record snapshot.\n- source: short note about where the jersey records came from.\n- records: playable jersey arithmetic records.\n\nDo not add a teams array to this file. Do not duplicate team fields from db/teams.json. Do not store city, playerNteam, playerNsport, or tgbids in records.\n\nRuntime contract:\n- The game selects records by team TGBID, not by city.\n- Each playable record stores player1tgbid, player2tgbid, and player3tgbid.\n- The runtime derives player team names, sports, colors, fanbase labels, display market, and de-duplicated tgbids from db/teams.json.\n- Do not invent TGBIDs. If a team is missing from db/teams.json, do not use that team until db/teams.json has a real permanent TGBID for it.\n\nRecord fields, in this order:\nplayer1name\nplayer1num\nplayer1tgbid\nplayer2name\nplayer2num\nplayer2tgbid\nplayer3name\nplayer3num\nplayer3tgbid\noperator\n\nGame equation:\nplayer1num operator player2num = player3num\n\nSupported operators:\n+ and - only.\n\nBatch scope:\n- A generation batch may cover up to ten target teams at a time.\n- Create enough rows that every requested target TGBID appears in at least one record.\n- Records may use one team, multiple teams from one market, or mixed teams from nearby sports markets when the equation is clean.\n\nNumber rules:\n- Jersey numbers must be integers from 0 through 99 only. Never use three-digit numbers.\n- 0 is allowed when the athlete actually wore 0 for the cited team.\n- Do not create equations with negative final jersey numbers.\n- The arithmetic must be exact.\n- Every jersey number must be the number the athlete actually wore with the team identified by that playerNtgbid. Players often switch numbers when they change teams, so never carry a number over from a different team.\n- A few players wore more than one number with the same team. Include these players when useful, but use the player's original/first number with that team unless there is a strong reason not to.\n\nPlayer rules:\n- Use famous or highly recognizable pro athletes.\n- Use full player names, first name plus last name. Do not use first-initial forms like S. Mills or surname-only records.\n- Common public initial names are okay when that is how the player is known, such as A.J. Bouye or C.J. Stroud.\n- Preserve familiar hyphenated names when appropriate.\n\nTeam and sport rules:\n- Choose teams by TGBID from db/teams.json.\n- Do not store playerNteam or playerNsport in records. Those are derived from db/teams.json.\n- Use all four major North American pro sports when a market supports them: NFL, NBA, MLB, and NHL.\n- Do not limit new records to teams already used by the game, but every used team must have a valid TGBID in db/teams.json.\n\nRecord quality:\n- Make each row a clean trivia-style equation, not a random set of obscure players.\n- Avoid duplicate equations and duplicate exact rows.\n- Keep a good mix of + and - operators.\n- Include multiple teams per market when possible, especially across football, basketball, baseball, and hockey.\n- All three jersey numbers must match the listed athletes and the teams identified by their TGBIDs.\n- Jersey 3 is the calculated answer, so player3 should be a satisfying known-player answer.\n\nValidation checklist before returning JSON:\n- Confirm every record has player1num operator player2num equal to player3num.\n- Confirm every number is 0 through 99.\n- Confirm every player name is a full name, not first-initial shorthand.\n- Confirm every playerNtgbid exists in db/teams.json.\n- Confirm every player's number matches the team identified by that TGBID.\n- Confirm no record stores city, playerNteam, playerNsport, tgbids, or a teams array.\n- Confirm no duplicate exact equations.\n- Confirm the JSON parses.\n- Preserve this _ai_update_prompt field unless the user explicitly asks to change the prompt.",
